{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (PATIENT): Burning.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Come through, have a seat. I'm Doctor Naidoo. Who's come with you?",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Lindi, her sister. She didn't want to come alone.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): What's bothering you today?",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (PATIENT): Burning.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (DOCTOR): Burning when you pass urine?",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (PATIENT): Ja.",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): She's in and out of the loo the whole time, night included.",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (DOCTOR): More often than usual, including at night?",
  "[SEG0010] person_1 (PATIENT): Ja.",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (DOCTOR): How long has the burning been going?",
  "[SEG0012] person_1 (PATIENT): Two.",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Ag, no. She was sore last Tuesday already. Nearly a week.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (DOCTOR): Is it two days or nearer a week?",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (PATIENT): Don't know.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (DOCTOR): Then I'll note roughly two days to a week, and that the two of you don't agree.",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (DOCTOR): How many times has this come back this year?",
  "[SEG0018] person_1 (PATIENT): Three.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): You forgot February, after the wedding.",
  "[SEG0020] person_1 (PATIENT): Maybe four.",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (DOCTOR): Possibly the fourth time this year, not the third. Alright.",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (DOCTOR): Did you take something for the burning?",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (PATIENT): Pills.",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): She swallowed two of my leftover amoxicillin capsules yesterday morning, for this, and the bottle's empty now.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (DOCTOR): Do you know the dose?",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I think they were five hundred milligrams. Not sure.",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (DOCTOR): Were you given nitrofurantoin after a previous infection?",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Nitrofurantoin, a hundred milligrams at night, for the March infection. She stopped after a few nights.",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (DOCTOR): When did you stop it?",
  "[SEG0030] person_1 (PATIENT): March.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Her stomach turned on it, so she left it.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (DOCTOR): Did you ever start the trimethoprim that was prescribed in June?",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (PATIENT): Never.",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): She never collected it from the chemist. Not one tablet.",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (DOCTOR): Then I won't put trimethoprim down as a medicine. Any vaginal discharge, or itching?",
  "[SEG0036] person_1 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0037] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): That's not quite true. She said last night it was itchy. She's embarrassed.",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (DOCTOR): Is there itching?",
  "[SEG0039] person_1 (PATIENT): Bit.",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any discharge, or just the itch?",
  "[SEG0041] person_1 (PATIENT): Itch.",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (DOCTOR): A bit of vaginal itch only, no discharge. We'll keep this straightforward.",
  "[SEG0043] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Yoh, the robot by the mall was out with load shedding. We sat in the bakkie forever.",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (DOCTOR): I was stuck in that same queue on the way in.",
  "[SEG0045] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): My grandson phoned about the cricket. He's six, mad about the Proteas.",
  "[SEG0046] person_2 (DOCTOR): Did they win? I missed the end.",
  "[SEG0047] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Last over. He screamed the house down and now he wants a new bat.",
  "[SEG0048] person_2 (DOCTOR): Rain's coming this weekend. They'll drag the covers on.",
  "[SEG0049] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): The sports shop queue was out the door too, lights going on and off.",
  "[SEG0050] person_2 (DOCTOR): Typical. Anyway, let's get back to you, Nomsa.",
  "[SEG0051] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any fever?",
  "[SEG0052] person_1 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0053] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any nausea or vomiting with this episode?",
  "[SEG0054] person_1 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0055] person_2 (DOCTOR): Pain over the kidneys?",
  "[SEG0056] person_1 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0057] person_2 (DOCTOR): Blood in the urine?",
  "[SEG0058] person_1 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0059] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any allergies to medicines?",
  "[SEG0060] person_1 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0061] person_2 (DOCTOR): I'm going to press on your tummy. Abdomen is soft, tender above the pubic bone, and the loins are not tender.",
  "[SEG0062] person_2 (DOCTOR): Your blood pressure is one-eighteen over seventy-four, pulse eighty-six, and your temperature is thirty-seven point two.",
  "[SEG0063] person_2 (DOCTOR): Let me say it back. Burning when you wee, passing urine often day and night, possibly a fourth episode this year, length somewhere between two days and a week, a bit of itch and no discharge.",
  "[SEG0064] person_1 (PATIENT): Ja.",
  "[SEG0065] person_2 (DOCTOR): You took two of your sister's amoxicillin capsules and stopped, and you stopped nitrofurantoin in March. No allergies.",
  "[SEG0066] person_1 (PATIENT): Ja.",
  "[SEG0067] person_2 (DOCTOR): This is most likely another bladder infection, cystitis, though the sample still has to confirm it.",
  "[SEG0068] person_2 (DOCTOR): I can't rule out thrush or simple irritation as the cause of the itch.",
  "[SEG0069] person_2 (DOCTOR): I'll send a midstream urine for microscopy and culture today.",
  "[SEG0070] person_2 (DOCTOR): I'll also give you fosfomycin, three grams, one sachet by mouth, once only, for the infection.",
  "[SEG0071] person_2 (DOCTOR): Please drink more water, and don't use somebody else's antibiotics again.",
  "[SEG0072] person_2 (DOCTOR): We might do a scan if it does not settle.",
  "[SEG0073] person_2 (DOCTOR): Let's see you in two weeks."
 ],
